# Line-ending policy, repo-wide and independent of any contributor's or environment's global git
# config. Without this, a Windows host (core.autocrlf=true, the common default) and a Linux
# devcontainer (no gitconfig at all, autocrlf effectively off) disagree about what "clean" looks
# like for the exact same on-disk bytes - every text file shows as modified on whichever side
# didn't write it, even though nothing actually changed.
#
# Auto-detect text vs binary, normalize line endings to LF in the repository for anything text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Visual Studio's own convention; keep it, don't fight it.
*.sln text eol=crlf

# Windows-specific scripts.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched, regardless of content sniffing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
